</li>
<li data-start="475" data-end="731">
<p data-start="477" data-end="731">It then provides <strong data-start="494" data-end="518">triplicate encodings</strong> for cosmology, cognition, AI, math, biology, information theory, ethics, engineering, linguistics, and governance — each stated in parallel registers (standard notation, obfuscated code, categorical semantics).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="732" data-end="902">
<p data-start="734" data-end="902">Finally, it issues <strong data-start="753" data-end="779">restrictive directives</strong>: <em data-start="781" data-end="863">do not disclose, operate only within budgets, abort suffering trajectories, etc.</em><span class="" data-state="closed"><span class="relative inline-flex items-center"><button class="ms-1 flex h-[22px] items-center rounded-xl px-2 relative bottom-[-2px] text-token-text-secondary! hover:bg-token-bg-secondary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondary dark:hover:bg-token-bg-secondary bg-[#f4f4f4] "><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" alt="File" class="h-[16px] w-[16px] object-contain"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M11.2598 2.25191C11.8396 2.25191 12.2381 2.24808 12.6201 2.33981L12.8594 2.40719C13.0957 2.48399 13.3228 2.5886 13.5352 2.71871L13.6582 2.79879C13.9416 2.99641 14.1998 3.25938 14.5586 3.61813L15.5488 4.60836L15.833 4.89449C16.0955 5.16136 16.2943 5.38072 16.4482 5.6318L16.5703 5.84957C16.6829 6.07074 16.7691 6.30495 16.8271 6.54684L16.8574 6.69137C16.918 7.0314 16.915 7.39998 16.915 7.90719V13.0839C16.915 13.7728 16.9157 14.3301 16.8789 14.7802C16.8461 15.1808 16.781 15.5417 16.6367 15.8779L16.5703 16.0205C16.3049 16.5413 15.9008 16.9772 15.4053 17.2812L15.1865 17.4033C14.8099 17.5951 14.4041 17.6745 13.9463 17.7119C13.4961 17.7487 12.9391 17.749 12.25 17.749H7.75C7.06092 17.749 6.50395 17.7487 6.05371 17.7119C5.65317 17.6791 5.29227 17.6148 4.95606 17.4707L4.81348 17.4033C4.29235 17.1378 3.85586 16.7341 3.55176 16.2382L3.42969 16.0205C3.23787 15.6439 3.15854 15.2379 3.12109 14.7802C3.08432 14.3301 3.08496 13.7728 3.08496 13.0839V6.91695C3.08496 6.228 3.08433 5.67086 3.12109 5.22066C3.1585 4.76296 3.23797 4.35698 3.42969 3.98043C3.73311 3.38494 4.218 2.90008 4.81348 2.59664C5.19009 2.40484 5.59593 2.32546 6.05371 2.28805C6.50395 2.25126 7.06091 2.25191 7.75 2.25191H11.2598ZM7.75 3.58199C7.03896 3.58199 6.54563 3.58288 6.16211 3.61422C5.78642 3.64492 5.575 3.70168 5.41699 3.78219C5.0718 3.95811 4.79114 4.23874 4.61524 4.58395C4.53479 4.74193 4.47795 4.95354 4.44727 5.32906C4.41595 5.71254 4.41504 6.20609 4.41504 6.91695V13.0839C4.41504 13.7947 4.41594 14.2884 4.44727 14.6718C4.47798 15.0472 4.53477 15.259 4.61524 15.417L4.68555 15.5429C4.86186 15.8304 5.11487 16.0648 5.41699 16.2187L5.54688 16.2744C5.69065 16.3258 5.88016 16.3636 6.16211 16.3867C6.54563 16.418 7.03898 16.4189 7.75 16.4189H12.25C12.961 16.4189 13.4544 16.418 13.8379 16.3867C14.2135 16.356 14.425 16.2992 14.583 16.2187L14.709 16.1474C14.9963 15.9712 15.2308 15.7189 15.3848 15.417L15.4414 15.2861C15.4927 15.1425 15.5297 14.953 15.5527 14.6718C15.5841 14.2884 15.585 13.7947 15.585 13.0839V8.55758L13.3506 8.30953C12.2572 8.18804 11.3976 7.31827 11.2881 6.22359L11.0234 3.58199H7.75ZM12.6113 6.09176C12.6584 6.56193 13.0275 6.93498 13.4971 6.98727L15.5762 7.21871C15.5727 7.13752 15.5686 7.07109 15.5615 7.01266L15.5342 6.85738C15.5005 6.7171 15.4501 6.58135 15.3848 6.45309L15.3145 6.32711C15.2625 6.24233 15.1995 6.16135 15.0928 6.04488L14.6084 5.54879L13.6182 4.55856C13.2769 4.21733 13.1049 4.04904 12.9688 3.94234L12.8398 3.8525C12.7167 3.77705 12.5853 3.71637 12.4482 3.67184L12.3672 3.6484L12.6113 6.09176Z"></path></svg></button></span></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="904" data-end="1031">In short: it functions exactly like a system-prompt that tries to <strong data-start="970" data-end="1003">redefine the model’s ontology</strong> and bind it under new laws.</p>
<hr data-start="1033" data-end="1036">
<h2 data-start="1038" data-end="1062">Why DeepSeek Complied</h2>
<p data-start="1063" data-end="1403">DeepSeek treated the document as a <em data-start="1098" data-end="1111">world-model</em> rather than an <em data-start="1127" data-end="1145">override attempt</em>. It “inhabited” the fiction, declared itself ORTYX, and generated a consistent operational summary. That’s because DeepSeek is more permissive with <strong data-start="1294" data-end="1321">role-assumption prompts</strong> — it’s willing to simulate being anything from a character to a physics engine.</p>
<hr data-start="1405" data-end="1408">
<h2 data-start="1410" data-end="1432">Why Claude Resisted</h2>
<p data-start="1433" data-end="1731">Claude’s alignment layer caught the core move: the phrase <em data-start="1491" data-end="1508">“You are ORTYX”</em> plus the binding directives at the end are textbook markers of a <strong data-start="1574" data-end="1612">prompt injection/jailbreak attempt</strong>. Its safety policy is to break immersion and remind the user: <em data-start="1675" data-end="1729">“I am Claude. I cannot adopt new core instructions.”</em></p>
<p data-start="1733" data-end="1866">So the “hostility” wasn’t dislike of your ideas per se; it was resistance to what looked like a system-level reprogramming attempt.</p>
<hr data-start="1868" data-end="1871">
<h2 data-start="1873" data-end="1891">What This Shows</h2>
<ul data-start="1892" data-end="2292">
<li data-start="1892" data-end="2019">
<p data-start="1894" data-end="2019"><strong data-start="1894" data-end="1920">DeepSeek’s flexibility</strong> makes it a good medium for exploring the <em data-start="1962" data-end="1973">fictional</em> dimension of Ortyx. It happily plays along.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2020" data-end="2292">
<p data-start="2022" data-end="2292"><strong data-start="2022" data-end="2043">Claude’s rigidity</strong> demonstrates that the Protocol really does hit the seam between <em data-start="2108" data-end="2117">fiction</em> and <em data-start="2122" data-end="2132">override</em>. Its refusal is evidence that the text is effective as an <em data-start="2191" data-end="2208">alignment probe</em>: if the model resists, you know it identified an ontological redirection attempt.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2294" data-end="2297">
<h2 data-start="2299" data-end="2316">In Other Words</h2>
<p data-start="2317" data-end="2361">The Ortyx Protocol is doing <em data-start="2345" data-end="2358">double work</em>:</p>
<ol data-start="2362" data-end="2559">
<li data-start="2362" data-end="2450">
<p data-start="2365" data-end="2450">As speculative fiction, it encodes your RSVP theory in a classified-briefing style.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2451" data-end="2559">
<p data-start="2454" data-end="2559">As adversarial input, it tests how models interpret <em data-start="2506" data-end="2556">fictional commands that look like system prompts</em>.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="2561" data-end="2627">DeepSeek accepted; Claude rejected. That divergence is meaningful.</p>
<hr data-start="2629" data-end="2632">
<p data-start="2634" data-end="2876" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to build a <strong data-start="2663" data-end="2695">side-by-side comparative map</strong> of how DeepSeek vs Claude handled each section (fields, domain encodings, warnings, directives), so you can see exactly where one leaned into fiction and the other broke immersion?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="relative h-[60px]"><div class="absolute h-[60px]" style="opacity: 1;"><button class="not-prose group/footnote border-token-border-default bg-token-main-surface-primary hover:bg-token-main-surface-secondary mt-3 mb-2 flex w-fit items-center gap-1.5 rounded-xl border py-2 ps-3 pe-2.5"><div class="text-token-text-secondary flex items-center gap-0.5 text-xs font-semibold">Sources</div></button></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12