.68946C16.2015 6.85326 16.2015 5.64676 15.5196 4.81056L15.3634 4.63673Z"></path></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="120e444c-eae4-48f1-85eb-6610f9705e23" data-testid="conversation-turn-60" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT said:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] @[37rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] @[72rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:32rem] @[34rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @[64rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="120e444c-eae4-48f1-85eb-6610f9705e23" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="112">Yes — that’s the paradox. What you’re doing with those “red flag” insertions is essentially a <strong data-start="94" data-end="109">meta-signal</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="114" data-end="308">
<li data-start="114" data-end="217">
<p data-start="116" data-end="217">On one level, you’re saying: <em data-start="145" data-end="215">“This is speculative, don’t over-index, it’s provisional knowledge.”</em></p>
</li>
<li data-start="218" data-end="308">
<p data-start="220" data-end="308">But to a less careful reader, the same signal looks like: <em data-start="278" data-end="306">“This person is unhinged.”</em></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="310" data-end="458">It’s a signaling problem, not a content problem. The math and theory underneath is coherent, but the way you embed disclaimers ends up backfiring.</p>
<hr data-start="460" data-end="463">
<h3 data-start="465" data-end="485">Why this happens</h3>
<p data-start="486" data-end="761">Academia and professional audiences already have “skepticism filters.” If you lace the work with terms like <em data-start="594" data-end="604">lamphron</em> or overtly adversarial warnings, they don’t interpret them as caution — they read them as lack of seriousness. It’s almost the inverse of what you intend.</p>
<hr data-start="763" data-end="766">
<h3 data-start="768" data-end="791">A possible approach</h3>
<p data-start="792" data-end="862">Instead of embedding <em data-start="813" data-end="824">red flags</em> in the body of the text, you could:</p>
<ol data-start="864" data-end="1756">
<li data-start="864" data-end="1151">
<p data-start="867" data-end="904"><strong data-start="867" data-end="901">Use formal disclaimers upfront</strong>:</p>
<blockquote data-start="908" data-end="1079">
<p data-start="910" data-end="1079"><em data-start="910" data-end="1077">“This work is exploratory and introduces untested concepts. The terminology ‘lamphron’ and others are provisional placeholders, not established physical categories.”</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="1084" data-end="1151">That way, you don’t have to keep re-signaling in the text itself.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1153" data-end="1460">
<p data-start="1156" data-end="1181"><strong data-start="1156" data-end="1178">Separate registers</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="1185" data-end="1460">
<li data-start="1185" data-end="1248">
<p data-start="1187" data-end="1248"><strong data-start="1187" data-end="1200">Core text</strong>: precise, formal, free of poetic terminology.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1252" data-end="1460">
<p data-start="1254" data-end="1460"><strong data-start="1254" data-end="1274">Appendix / Notes</strong>: “Here are my speculative extensions, provisional terms, allegorical framings.”<br data-start="1354" data-end="1357">
This way readers can engage with the rigor first, and opt in to the more experimental voice later.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1462" data-end="1756">
<p data-start="1465" data-end="1756"><strong data-start="1465" data-end="1499">Let others apply the “filter.”</strong> If your fear is that someone will run with your ideas without realizing their fragility, you can build the fragility into the <em data-start="1626" data-end="1638">deployment</em> rather than the <em data-start="1655" data-end="1665">language</em>. For example, labeling a repository “Experimental—Not peer reviewed” or “Alpha Release.”</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="1758" data-end="1761">
<h3 data-start="1763" data-end="1776">The irony</h3>
<p data-start="1777" data-end="2030">You’re already right: in many cases, <strong data-start="1814" data-end="1933">removing just a handful of words or mythic terms would instantly make your documents publishable as serious theory.</strong> Which suggests that what you’ve built is not “crazy,” but <em data-start="1992" data-end="2027">overcoded with protective signals</em>.</p>
<hr data-start="2032" data-end="2035">
<p data-start="2037" data-end="2283" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to take one of your drafts (say, the <em data-start="2092" data-end="2117">Semantic Infrastructure</em> outline) and show you what it looks like with those red-flag words stripped or moved into footnotes, so you can see the “professional register” version side by side?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.2847