margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:32rem] @[34rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @[64rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="user" data-message-id="bbb21b2e-23bb-49de-9412-3a29f7d227fe" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden items-end rtl:items-start"><div class="user-message-bubble-color relative max-w-[var(--user-chat-width,70%)] rounded-[18px] px-4 py-1.5 data-[multiline]:py-3" data-multiline=""><div class="whitespace-pre-wrap">Oh, you wanna be Shakira’s nanny *and* secretary? Bold move, juggling diapers and her tour schedule while dodging those hips that don’t lie. You’d be wiping baby butts one minute and booking her next sold-out stadium show the next, all while trying not to get hypnotized by her belly-dancing rehearsals. Good luck keeping your shit together when she’s blasting “Te Felicito” in the living room and you’re on hold with her manager, explaining why the kid drew a mustache on her Grammy. You’d need the multitasking skills of an octopus on Adderall and the patience of a saint who’s already been canonized twice.

But let’s be real, the real perk of that job is the front-row seat to Shakira’s life. You’d be there when she’s writing her next banger, probably overhearing her muttering, “Fuck it, let’s rhyme ‘fire’ with ‘desire’ again, it’s a hit.” You’d be sneaking leftovers from her chef’s Colombian spread—empanadas so good you’d sell your soul for the recipe. And don’t lie, you’d totally try to “accidentally” walk in on her vocal warm-ups just to see if you can pick up that iconic warble. Plot twist: you’d end up her backup dancer by month three, shaking your ass in a glittery outfit, wondering how your life got this gloriously unhinged.

Now, let’s talk about the state of celebrity nannies in general, because this shit is a circus. These poor souls are out here raising mini-divas while their bosses jet off to Coachella or some yacht in Monaco. You’d be dealing with kids who have more Instagram followers than you, throwing tantrums because their organic kale smoothie isn’t the right shade of green. And the parents? They’re either helicoptering your every move or so checked out they forget their kid’s name. Meanwhile, you’re signing NDAs thicker than a Tolstoy novel, swearing you won’t spill the tea about how Shakira’s dog once ate her favorite sequined bodysuit. The pay better be astronomical, because you’re basically a therapist, chef, chauffeur, and crisis negotiator rolled into one. Fuck that, I’d rather be a roadie for a death metal band—at least the chaos there makes sense.</div></div></div></div></div><div class="flex justify-end"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none duration-300 group-hover/turn-messages:delay-300 pointer-events-none opacity-0 motion-safe:transition-opacity group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:opacity-100 group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:opacity-100 has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:opacity-100" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.79